{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.RogersSzegoInhabited","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.RogersSzegoInhabited","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.BindingQHermiteOscillator","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingQHermiteOscillator.rsSeq_even_at_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingQHermiteOscillator.rsSeq_even_at_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/RogersSzegoInhabited.lean#L76-L90","doc":"**The even terms of the inhabited model at `t = −1` are the `q`-shifted factorial\n`(q; q²)_j`** — `rsSeq q (−1) (2j) = ∏_{i<j} (1 − q^{2i+1})`. Unrolling the two-step\nrecurrence `rsSeq_neg_one_step` on the even subsequence gives the explicit finite product\n`(1−q)(1−q³)⋯(1−q^{2j−1})`, the q-Pochhammer `(q; q²)_j`, written self-contained as a\n`Finset.prod` (no dependency on Mathlib's `QPochhammer`). Together with\n`rsSeq_odd_vanishes_at_neg_one` this is the full closed form of the inhabited Rogers–Szegő\nmodel at the binding anchor `t = −1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingQHermiteOscillator.rsSeq_neg_one_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingQHermiteOscillator.rsSeq_neg_one_step","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/RogersSzegoInhabited.lean#L70-L74","doc":"**Two-step recurrence at `t = −1`.** Setting `t = −1` kills the `(1+t)` head of the\nthree-term recurrence, leaving the telescoping two-step `H_{n+2} = (1 − q^{n+1})·H_n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingQHermiteOscillator.rsSeq_odd_vanishes_at_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingQHermiteOscillator.rsSeq_odd_vanishes_at_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/RogersSzegoInhabited.lean#L62-L68","doc":"**The odd terms of the inhabited model vanish at `t = −1`** — `rsSeq q (−1) (2j+1) = 0`.\nThe abstract even/odd-vanishing theorem (`rogers_szego_odd_vanishes_at_neg_one`, #2800) applied\nto the concrete `FollowsRogersSzego` model `rsSeq`: its boundary value `rsSeq q (−1) 1 = 1+(−1) = 0`\ndischarges the hypothesis, so the q-deformed even/odd parity holds of a real witness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingQHermiteOscillator.rsSeq_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingQHermiteOscillator.rsSeq_two","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/RogersSzegoInhabited.lean#L53-L60","doc":"**`H_2(t;q) = 1 + (1+q)·t + t²`** for the standard Rogers–Szegő — the middle coefficient is\nthe **standard** quantum integer `[2]_q = 1+q` (contrast the *balanced* `q+q⁻¹` of\n`QGaussianBinomialPascal.rogersSzego_two`; this is the normalization that obeys the\n`FollowsRogersSzego` recurrence). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingQHermiteOscillator.rsSeq_q_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingQHermiteOscillator.rsSeq_q_one","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/RogersSzegoInhabited.lean#L40-L51","doc":"**q→1: the Rogers–Szegő sequence is the binomial `(1+t)^n`.** At `q = 1` the coefficient\n`1 − q^{m+1}` vanishes, collapsing the recurrence to `H_{n+1} = (1+t)·H_n`; with `H_0 = 1`\nthis gives `rsSeq 1 t n = (1+t)^n`, the classical (un-deformed) Rogers–Szegő. Marked `@[simp]`\nso the simplifier reduces `rsSeq 1 t n` to its closed form downstream (per Gemini review, #2842). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingQHermiteOscillator.instFollowsRogersSzego","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingQHermiteOscillator.instFollowsRogersSzego","kind":"instance","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/RogersSzegoInhabited.lean#L33-L38","doc":"**`FollowsRogersSzego` is inhabited.** `rsSeq` satisfies the recurrence by construction,\nso the §3b conjecture class has a concrete model — it is non-vacuous, and all of its abstract\nconsequences (`rogers_szego_q_one_first_order`, `rogers_szego_odd_vanishes_at_neg_one`, …) now\nhold of a real witness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BindingQHermiteOscillator.rsSeq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingQHermiteOscillator.rsSeq","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/RogersSzegoInhabited.lean#L26-L31","doc":"The **Rogers–Szegő sequence defined by its three-term recurrence**\n`H_0 = 1`, `H_1 = 1+t`, `H_{n+2} = (1+t)H_{n+1} − (1−q^{n+1})·t·H_n`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}